      "confidence": 0.9,
      "file_path": "src/handlers.js",
      "line_number": 6,
      "line_end": 6,
      "title": "Async onSave breaks the synchronous dispatch caller",
      "description": "onSave now returns a Promise, but dispatch in src/router.js:7 returns it without awaiting. The handler in src/main.js:9 then passes that Promise to res.end, which accepts only a string or Buffer. res.end throws a type error on every POST /save request, and the uncaught exception crashes the server. No caller handles a writeFile rejection, so it becomes an unhandled rejection. Make dispatch and the request handler async, and await the result before calling res.end. Catch errors in the request handler and answer with a 500 status.",
      "suggested_change": null,
      "source": "lens:async-floating-promise",
      "candidate": null,
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "onSave now returns a Promise, but dispatch in src/router.js:7 returns it without awaiting. The handler in src/main.js:9 then passes that Promise to res.end, which accepts only a string or Buffer.",
      "consequence": "res.end throws a type error on every POST /save request, and the uncaught exception crashes the server. No caller handles a writeFile rejection, so it becomes an unhandled rejection.",
      "fix": "Make dispatch and the request handler async, and await the result before calling res.end. Catch errors in the request handler and answer with a 500 status."
    },
    {
      "origin": "agent",
      "severity": "minor",
      "category": "maintainability",
